    "sobre": {
      "titulo": {
        "en": "About",
        "pt": ""
      },
      "lead": {
        "en": "Motion designer and editor based in São Paulo.",
        "pt": ""
      },
      "texto": {
        "en": "I'm Igor Romana. I studied graphic design at Belas Artes and have spent over ten years animating and cutting in agencies and production companies. With the agency Cappuccino, I animate and edit for Carrefour, Ajinomoto, Blowtex and Universal. Before that, I worked on campaigns for Globo, Samsung, Jack Daniel's, Budweiser, Decathlon, AXA Seguros and Banco Santander, and on films for Neve and Gloob.\n\nI start on paper and think about the whole pipeline. I've drawn since I was six, and because I animate and edit, I draw already knowing how a frame will move and where it will be cut. Outside client work I paint, and I've shown in group exhibitions in São Paulo. Years behind a drum kit gave me discipline and an ear for timing.\n\nI work remotely on GMT-3, which overlaps well with Europe and the Americas.",
        "pt": ""
      },
