      "ia_titulo": {
        "en": "How I use AI",
        "pt": ""
      },
      "ia": {
        "en": "AI gives my work structure and room to grow. It takes on research, references, first directions and quick tests, and that frees the hours I need to build the context myself, with my own line and my own ideas. I use it as a real assistant: one that lets me push limits fast and on my own terms.\n\nThis site is an example. I planned it with Claude: the case interviews, a map of the project, the design system, the first drafts of this copy. For clients, the same method means more tests, with clear direction.\n\nDay to day, I use a video compressor I built with it, and it keeps my schedule in order. Now testing: prompt workflows for video and AI-assisted editing.\n\nThere is a line I keep. The drawing, the idea and the final call are mine. AI suggests; I decide what stays.",
        "pt": ""
      },
      "arte_titulo": {
        "en": "Outside client work,\nI paint.",
        "pt": ""
      },
      "arte_texto": {
        "en": "Oil and encaustic on canvas, in series. The same hand that draws the storyboards.",
        "pt": ""
      },
